This Python function should remove all even numbers from a list, but it gives wrong results for some inputs. Trace it by hand on [2, 4, 6, 1] and [1, 2, 2, 3], explain why it fails, then give two different fixes and check both on the same inputs:

def remove_evens(nums):
    for i in range(len(nums)):
        if i < len(nums) and nums[i] % 2 == 0:
            nums.pop(i)
    return nums
